            <h2>1. Designated Copyright Agent</h2>
            <p>Pursuant to 17 U.S.C. § 512(c), notifications of claimed copyright infringement should be sent to our Designated Copyright Agent:</p>
            <p>
                <strong>Designated DMCA Compliance Agent</strong><br>
                Stream Helper Legal Operations<br>
                Email: <a href="mailto:dmca@streamhelper.app">dmca@streamhelper.app</a><br>
                Response Time: Within 24–48 business hours
            </p>

            <h2>2. Elements of a Valid DMCA Notice</h2>
            <p>To ensure prompt processing of any copyright inquiry, notifications must be provided in writing and contain the following statutory requirements:</p>
            <ol>
                <li>A physical or electronic signature of a person authorized to act on behalf of the owner of an exclusive right that is allegedly infringed.</li>
                <li>Identification of the copyrighted work claimed to have been infringed, or, if multiple copyrighted works are covered by a single notification, a representative list of such works.</li>
                <li>Identification of the specific material (such as documentation, software links, or project code) that is claimed to be infringing or to be the subject of infringing activity, and information reasonably sufficient to permit us to locate the material.</li>
                <li>Information reasonably sufficient to permit our team to contact you, such as an address, telephone number, and email address.</li>
                <li>A statement that you have a good faith belief that use of the material in the manner complained of is not authorized by the copyright owner, its agent, or the law.</li>
                <li>A statement that the information in the notification is accurate, and under penalty of perjury, that you are authorized to act on behalf of the owner of an exclusive right that is allegedly infringed.</li>
            </ol>

            <h2>3. Counter-Notification Procedures</h2>
            <p>If material has been removed or disabled as a result of a DMCA notification and you believe this was due to mistake or misidentification, you may submit a written counter-notification pursuant to 17 U.S.C. § 512(g)(3) containing your contact information, signature, identification of the removed material, and consent to legal jurisdiction.</p>

            <h2>4. Repeat Infringer Policy</h2>
            <p>In accordance with the DMCA and other applicable intellectual property laws, we maintain a policy of terminating accounts or revoking service access for users who repeatedly or egregiously infringe the intellectual property rights of others.</p>
